        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c1429585-4985-5088-b0ef-9a9b7d0decfd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: APB, Sleeper, South\n- People: Louise Wener, Rocco Giordano, Josh Swade\n- Companies: Young American Recordings, Kinetic Records, Maverick Records\n- Places: Scotland, England, London\n- Genres: post-punk, funk rock, punk rock, new wave, Britpop\n- Works: Trainspotting\n\nFacts:\n- APB was a Scottish post-punk band formed in 1979 that blended funk rock, punk rock, and new wave music.\n- Sleeper was an English Britpop band formed in London and fronted by Louise Wener.\n- During the 1990s, Sleeper had eight UK Top 40 hit singles and three UK Top 10 albums, and Sleeper's music was featured in the soundtrack of the film Trainspotting.\n- Young American Recordings was founded by Rocco Giordano of Kinetic Records and Josh Swade of Maverick Records as an independent label.\n- Young American Recordings included the British rock band South and worked with the Scottish punk band APB.\n- APB had only modest success during its brief run, but APB influenced later bands including Franz Ferdinand, The Rapture, and Red Hot Chili Peppers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "63d9e1c4-4ac9-51e7-8aa9-78a1b094eb7f",
        "text": "Page: APB (band). Sentence: APB was a Scottish post-punk band, formed in 1979, that blended funk rock, punk rock and new wave music.\nPage: APB (band). Sentence: The group had only modest success during its brief run, yet their influence can be heard in the sound of such current bands as Franz Ferdinand, The Rapture, and Red Hot Chili Peppers.\nPage: Sleeper (band). Sentence: Sleeper are an English Britpop band, fronted by Louise Wener and formed in London.\nPage: Sleeper (band). Sentence: The group had eight UK Top 40 hit singles and three UK Top 10 albums during the 1990s Their music was also featured in the soundtrack of the pop cultural hit movie \"Trainspotting\".\nPage: Young American Recordings. Sentence: Founded by Rocco Giordano of Kinetic Records and Josh Swade of Maverick Records, it was an independent label that included groups such as British rock band South and worked with other popular groups such as Scottish punk band APB.",
